{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The adjustable power supply and 220 ohm resistors would help me test and build circuits with my breadboards, relay module and LEDs, so they feel like useful next purchases.",
    "The magnet wire connects directly to my earlier ferrite toroid cores because I could use them together to wind coils. That specific connection makes it more relevant than a general electronics accessory."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The brass rods, AC motor controller and specialized test leads assume projects or equipment I have not shown a need for. My component purchases do not mean I currently need machining materials or every kind of electrical tool.",
    "Fast blinking LEDs do not serve the same purpose as simple circuit indicators, and solder paste does not fit the breadboard and through-hole work reflected in my purchases."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seem to treat a broad connection to electronics or workshop work as enough, even when an item would not help with the circuits I am interested in building.",
    "They seem to assume that buying LEDs makes another bulk LED pack useful, without distinguishing decorative blinking lights from practical indicators or considering the LEDs already included in my kit."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "I am more interested in items that complete a plausible project, such as wire for my toroid cores or resistors for LED experiments, than in loosely related supplies.",
    "An item can fit my interests without being something I would buy today: I already have some LEDs, and I would choose only one power supply, favoring the KAIWEETS display and USB interface this time."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in circuit building but sometimes confuse a broad electronics connection with a specific, useful next purchase."
}"}
